From b038999c8d040e3d65ca96274dcb0e7c40443c1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AOSP RK3576 Baseline <uhf-platform@localbuild>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 10:07:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Brand boot splash with ID TECH Identity and Security logo

Replaces the stock U-Boot splash (logo.bmp) and kernel fbcon splash
(logo_kernel.bmp) with the ID TECH "Identity and Security" logo,
reconstructed to the exact 654x270 8bpp indexed BMP format this board's
boot chain requires (kernel-6.1/scripts/mkimg packs both into
resource.img; the board dtsi references them via logo,uboot / logo,kernel
under each display node).

Both files are covered, not just logo.bmp, so the branding is continuous
across the whole pre-Android boot sequence: U-Boot's own splash, then the
kernel's fbcon splash, with no stock-logo gap between them before
Android's boot animation takes over.

Format notes:
- 654x270 to match the existing stock bitmaps exactly (this is fixed by
  the display panel's boot-splash region, not a free choice).
- Saved uncompressed (BI_RGB) rather than RLE8 like the stock bitmaps.
  Confirmed against u-boot/drivers/video/video_bmp.c that the decoder's
  8bpp path supports plain BI_RGB directly - RLE8 is a separate,
  optional branch (CONFIG_VIDEO_BMP_RLE8), not a requirement - so this
  is a supported format, just a larger file (~173KB vs ~12-21KB).
- The artwork itself is a reconstruction from the reference logo image
  (not a pixel copy of a source file), built programmatically to hit
  this exact resolution: black/blue ID|TECH lockup plus the gray
  IDENTITY AND SECURITY strip, using DejaVu Sans Bold with manual letter
  spacing on the bottom strip to match the source's tracked-out look.

Unverified: not boot-tested on hardware in this environment (no device
attached here). The BMP format and dimensions are verified against the
board's own decoder and mkimg script; visual centering/proportions
should be confirmed on a real panel and adjusted (crop/letterbox) if the
panel's aspect ratio differs from 654x270's.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
